sic” and “TDTNTOR 2” cabins in order to place the TDTNTOR 2 cabin closer to the spawn\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eCredits\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003ePolishing + QoL\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAdded a UI button to skip to the end of the cutscene\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAdded a door to teleport to TDTNTOR 2\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003eBug Fixes + Performance\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eImproved the underlying logic for the ending cutscene\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eImproved the reliability of playing various music tracks at the right time\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\nTDTNTOR 2 Patch Notes\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cem\\u003eThe intent of this patch is to counter Roblox’s changes to the discovery algorithm which leave TDTNTOR in the dust.\\u003c/em\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eLobby\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003ePolishing + QoL\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAdded a shop which contains all of TDTNTOR 2’s gamepasses + merch items\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAdded localization support developer products to the above shop - all proceeds of these products go directly to the localization expert\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAdded several noob-themed accessories to the above shop\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eReorganized the order of the “Bonus Chapter” doors to more easily convey the chronological order of the extended storyline\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eConverted the “TDTNTOR Classic” door into a VHS tape\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eConverted the “Cloakedyoshi’s Noob Defense” door into a VHS tape\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003ePurchasing a gamepass for a bonus chapter no longer automatically teleports you into that chapter\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eScraped new strings for localization\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003eBug Fixes + Performance\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eFixed clipping issues with the puddle outside the “The Fate of Blink” door on low graphics\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eChapter One\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003ePolishing + QoL\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eVisually enhanced the exterior of the police station\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003eBug Fixes + Performance\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eFixed a bug where the bloxMart music would stutter if a player walked across bloxMart’s roof\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eEnding Three\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003eBug Fixes + Performance\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eImproved the underlying logic for the ending cutscene\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eChapter Zero\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003ePolishing + QoL\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eVisually enhanced the exterior of the police station\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eSource Code\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003ch4\\u003ePolishing + QoL\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eThe chapter exit for Source Code now teleports into TDTNTOR 3\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003e\\u003ca name=\\\&quot;p-7560495-h-12252022-patch-10-12\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;anchor\\\&quot; href=\\\&quot;#p-7560495-h-12252022-patch-10-12\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u0