              <h1><a name="p-6955951-h-03132022-the-i-cant-hear-you-update-1" class="anchor" href="#p-6955951-h-03132022-the-i-cant-hear-you-update-1"></a>03/13/2022 - The “I Can’t Hear You” Update <img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/musical_note.png?v=14" title=":musical_note:" class="emoji" alt=":musical_note:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"></h1>
<details>
<summary>
Update Log</summary>
<p><div class="lightbox-wrapper"><a class="lightbox" href="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/original/5X/9/c/8/4/9c84bc244c042f8cc3f01fbc05abcdf2a35221a9.jpeg" data-download-href="/uploads/short-url/mkCRR8QqwoTF2r0rU3iQk7dXHER.jpeg?dl=1" title="RobloxScreenShot20220313_001750509" rel="noopener nofollow ugc"><img src="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/9/c/8/4/9c84bc244c042f8cc3f01fbc05abcdf2a35221a9_2_690x388.jpeg" alt="RobloxScreenShot20220313_001750509" data-base62-sha1="rOhHM6QfIjWKZ2PLGrXUx02NQbe" width="690" height="388" data-dominant-color="5F5247" srcset="//devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/9/c/8/4/9c84bc244c042f8cc3f01fbc05abcdf2a35221a9_2_690x388.jpeg, //devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/9/c/8/4/9c84bc244c042f8cc3f01fbc05abcdf2a35221a9_2_1035x582.jpeg 1.5x, //devforum-uploads.s3.dualstack.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/optimized/5X/9/c/8/4/9c84bc244c042f8cc3f01fbc05abcdf2a35221a9_2_1380x776.jpeg 2x"><div class="meta"><svg class="fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#far-image"></use></svg><span class="filename">RobloxScreenShot20220313_001750509</span><span class="informations">1920×1080 93.7 KB</span><svg class="fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#discourse-expand"></use></svg></div></a></div><br>
<em>Some sounds are going poof - but that’s a great excuse for me to have some fun with some polish…</em></p>
<h1><a name="p-6955951-update-log-2" class="anchor" href="#p-6955951-update-log-2"></a>Update Log</h1>
<blockquote>
<h3>Overall</h3>
<h4>Highlights</h4>
<ul>
<li>Added some neat little easter eggs and details to various chapters</li>
<li>Against my better judgement, re-enabled in-game bug reports for most chapters</li>
<li>Replaced sounds that will be removed by <a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/t/action-needed-upcoming-changes-to-asset-privacy-for-audio/1701697">the upcoming Roblox update</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Restored NPC idle animations; <a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/t/animation-engine-runtime-changes-and-fixes/1320674">they were broken from a Roblox update</a></li>
<li>Removed unused SFX from the options UI</li>
</ul>
<h4>Polishing + QoL</h4>
<ul>
<li>Ensured TDTNTOR 2’s sounds will still make sense with <a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/t/the-volumetric-sounds-beta-is-here/1695240/">the upcoming Roblox volumetric sounds update</a></li>
<li>Sitting NPCs now bob up and down</li>
<li>Improved TDTNTOR 2’s ban system</li>
<li>Scraped new strings for localization</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter One <img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"><img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"><img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"><img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"><img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"><img src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/duck.png?v=14" title=":duck:" class="emoji" alt=":duck:" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20"></h3>
<h4>Polishing + QoL</h4>
<ul>
<li>Added new sounds to the ducks; special thanks to <a class="mention" href="/u/dudeax">@DudeAx</a> for the most tubular duck beat</li>
<li>Added a new NPC with dialog</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>The bloxMart clerk now periodically sighs when being spoken to</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>The deli owner now fruitlessly attempts to open a can of noob fish when being spoken to - it’s his only remaining ingredient, after all</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Officer Brooke occasionally sips a refreshing coffee</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Officer Connors has decided to stand at her desk; she now also uses her computer keyboard to stay productive</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Chief Rodgers is still just chilling… but he has some interesting papers on his desk…</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>The mayor has adopted a flair for the dramatic</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>Running NPCs with dialog hints are now more responsive to stop when their dialog is activated</li>
</ul>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>bloxMart’s music now respects a player’s music volume setting</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter One/Two Transition</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Noobs now properly respawn again after exiting the city</li>
<li>You can no longer see respawned noobs’ super top secret names</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter Two</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Opening the armory door now properly plays a success SFX again</li>
<li>Falling into the training pool now properly plays a splash SFX again</li>
<li>Removed unused sounds</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter Three</h3>
<h4>Balancing</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Redesigned Prince Noob and Princess Noob’s attacks</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p> Reduced Prince and Princess Noob’s sword lengths from 5.2 studs to 4.2 studs</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Prince Noob now slows down when slashing his sword</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>Reduced Prince Noob’s idle blade damage from 1 HP to .5 HP</li>
<li>Reduced Prince Noob’s twirl attack damage from 20 HP to 15 HP</li>
<li>Increased Prince Noob’s twirl attack duration by 1.2 seconds</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Prince Noob now has a short period of dizziness after his twirl attack</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Princess Noob’s attack pattern is now slightly more formulaic instead of pure random</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>Reduced the lethality of Princess Noob’s sword when she is not swinging it from 35 HP to .5 HP</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Increased Princess Noob’s minimum leaping swings from 1 to 3</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Reduced Princess Noob’s maximum leaping swings from 10 to 5</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Princess Noob’s falling kicks are now deadly</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Princess Noob has taken a page out of her brother’s playbook and now has the ability to charge with her sword</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>Simplified player spawning in Princess Noob’s arena</li>
</ul>
<h4>Polishing + QoL</h4>
<ul>
<li>Visually enhanced Prince Noob’s castle</li>
<li>
<div class="spoiler">
<p>Prince Noob and Princess Noob now have custom dialog when hurt</p>
</div>
</li>
<li>Improved Prince Noob and Princess Noob’s animations + FX</li>
<li>Did some organizational management to make future updates easier</li>
</ul>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Fixed some visual clipping on a hiker’s tent</li>
<li>Anchored some unanchored mountain bricks</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter Five</h3>
<h4>Balancing</h4>
<ul>
<li>Decreased the cooldown time it takes to press the door puzzle’s buttons (3 seconds to 1.5 seconds)</li>
</ul>
<h4>Polishing + QoL</h4>
<ul>
<li>The door puzzle is now client-side</li>
<li>Recoded the door puzzle from scratch</li>
</ul>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>The door puzzle’s button hitboxes are now accurate</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Finale Talk</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Queen Noob now properly falls apart when murdered</li>
<li>Removed unused content</li>
<li>Various sounds now have proper sound falloff</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Finale Fight</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Various sounds now have proper sound falloff</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Ending One</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Restored the crowd celebration FX</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>The Cannery</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Various sounds now have proper sound falloff</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Welcome to Banland</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Various sounds now have proper sound falloff</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Missing Piece</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Snowball Cannon Noobs, Snowball Noobs, and Coal Noobs now properly shoot projectiles again</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Doomsday</h3>
<h4>Bug Fixes + Performance</h4>
<ul>
<li>Removed unused SFX</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<h3>Chapter Zero</h3>
<h4>Polishing + QoL</h4>
<ul>
<li>Carried over new duck logic + SFX from Chapter One</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
</details>
<details>
